{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible","id":866037,"title":"Using Protean to steal the visage of a human possible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T12:01:03-07:00","id":866037,"title":"Using Protean to steal the visage of a human possible?","content":"It says to take on a new animal shape, one must fully feed on the animal, killing it. Using protean 5 mist form, if you enter a human's lungs and feed from them fully, killing them.. would you not satisfy the requirements and after slumbering in your grave for a day and night, take on the form of the slain human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:17:58-07:00","id":866043,"title":"","content":"Do you consider, symbolically, humans to be:<br /> a) predatory animals<br /> b) carrion-eaters<br /> c) parasites<br /> ?<br /> I would, personally, only allow it for a Vampire who is so far removed from Humanity that they don't consider humans more than animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:19:32-07:00","id":866044,"title":"","content":"Humans are a special case. Note that Animalism doesn't normally effect humans unless it specifies directly, but you can't Undead Familiar or Summon the Hunt, for example, on people. Protean would follow that same case.<br /> <br /> You want to look at the Devotion &quot;Drawing Upon the Mask&quot; under the Empusae (Gangrel) bloodline (Night Horrors - Immortal Sinners book). This lets you combine Obfuscate and Protean to physically shift your appearance.<br /> <br /> Also, check with your ST if a 'misted' vampire can fit in a pair of lungs. I, personally, wouldn't let it fly, but your table may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:20:31-07:00","id":866045,"title":"","content":"Human beings are omnivores, they eat spoiled food from trash cans and feed off others in some form or another. For an Ordo Gangrel, he very well might consider human beings to be a sort of animal, as well as a follower of Darwin and Evolution. I can see it being possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:23:21-07:00","id":866048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866044#post866044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans are a special case. Note that Animalism doesn't normally effect humans unless it specifies directly, but you can't Undead Familiar or Summon the Hunt, for example, on people. Protean would follow that same case.<br /> <br /> You want to look at the Devotion &quot;Drawing Upon the Mask&quot; under the Empusae (Gangrel) bloodline (Night Horrors - Immortal Sinners book). This lets you combine Obfuscate and Protean to physically shift your appearance.<br /> <br /> Also, check with your ST if a 'misted' vampire can fit in a pair of lungs. I, personally, wouldn't let it fly, but your table may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I should note that we are playing a 2nd edition campaign. In the new edition of vampire, it specifically says you can force your way into a human's lungs and feed that way, its a gruesome act but works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:32:37-07:00","id":866055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866048#post866048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note that we are playing a 2nd edition campaign. In the new edition of vampire, it specifically says you can force your way into a human's lungs and feed that way, its a gruesome act but works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had completely missed that line of the power, that <i>is</i> pretty gruesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:40:01-07:00","id":866057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866055#post866055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had completely missed that line of the power, that <i>is</i> pretty gruesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It really is. We are playing now and I am going to use it on some soldiers soon.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:56:37-07:00","id":866064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866043#post866043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you consider, symbolically, humans to be:<br /> a) predatory animals<br /> b) carrion-eaters<br /> c) parasites<br /> ?<br /> I would, personally, only allow it for a Vampire who is so far removed from Humanity that they don't consider humans more than animals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A.) While I do agree that humans are predators, I do not agree that we are predatory ANIMALS. Lions, tigers, bears, wolves, are predatory animals. I would not add a human to that list. We are not the same. We are sentient beings.<br /> <br /> B) as a whole Humans do not eat dead.. rotting things we found. Should we eat meat most of us do it in a dignified way.. after it's been cooked.<br /> <br /> C) we do not require a host Body to thrive. That's out.<br /> <br /> If you want to take on someone else's face. I would suggest transmutation blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> As WHW suggestion, I would only allow it if that character was so far gone that humans are nothing more than a monkey.. ( if at all )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:56:43-07:00","id":866099,"title":"","content":"It is, however, a very interesting villain concept; a classical trope of &quot;what a monster he became&quot;. High ranked Ordo who hovers at Humanity 1 or 2 might bring a very chilling plot point - for him, this application of the power works (and so does animalism; let's say he is a special NPC snowflake, mmkay?), but it doesn't for anyone else. Why? Is it because they are inhuman? Or is it because there is something special about them? A bloodline? A Coil? Something to do with Riding the Wave? It might be a Mystery, but it's certainly a mystery. <br /> This would be very chilling, because if he was a functional member of Kindred society, he could represent a dangerous proposition - that Humanity is, indeed, something that holds you back, and he is a undying proof of it. So other people might try to follow him, and become like him (and, because noone understands what makes him special, probably fail miserably at it). I think it's a great concept for City-Important Ordo NPC who isn't a politician, and might be even a pretty cool charming guy (who eats babies for science). <br /> Both classical Serial Killer IN The Shadows Cannibal Grangel and Ordo Eater sound cool. It wouldn't belong on players side of table at my games, but that's mostly because we don't play characters so removed from Humanity.<br /> <br /> As for actual rules, I don't think there is a point for trying to lawyer your way about humans being technically animals; Vampire Disciplines operate purely on symbolism, no science, and Humans and Animals are symbolically very different. I think allowing to do it would be against spirit of the Discipline, unless above paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:42:05-07:00","id":866127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866099#post866099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is, however, a very interesting villain concept; a classical trope of &quot;what a monster he became&quot;. High ranked Ordo who hovers at Humanity 1 or 2 might bring a very chilling plot point - for him, this application of the power works (and so does animalism; let's say he is a special NPC snowflake, mmkay?), but it doesn't for anyone else. Why? Is it because they are inhuman? Or is it because there is something special about them? A bloodline? A Coil? Something to do with Riding the Wave? It might be a Mystery, but it's certainly a mystery.<br /> This would be very chilling, because if he was a functional member of Kindred society, he could represent a dangerous proposition - that Humanity is, indeed, something that holds you back, and he is a undying proof of it. So other people might try to follow him, and become like him (and, because noone understands what makes him special, probably fail miserably at it). I think it's a great concept for City-Important Ordo NPC who isn't a politician, and might be even a pretty cool charming guy (who eats babies for science).<br /> Both classical Serial Killer IN The Shadows Cannibal Grangel and Ordo Eater sound cool. It wouldn't belong on players side of table at my games, but that's mostly because we don't play characters so removed from Humanity.<br /> <br /> As for actual rules, I don't think there is a point for trying to lawyer your way about humans being technically animals; Vampire Disciplines operate purely on symbolism, no science, and Humans and Animals are symbolically very different. I think allowing to do it would be against spirit of the Discipline, unless above paragraph.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great advice and I think I am going this route also. My friend and I are doing a round robin style game and we seem to agree on this. I love the idea of the soul sucker you envision, might make for a great NPC. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T17:34:42-07:00","id":866180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible#post866037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says to take on a new animal shape, one must fully feed on the animal, killing it. Using protean 5 mist form, if you enter a human's lungs and feed from them fully, killing them.. would you not satisfy the requirements and after slumbering in your grave for a day and night, take on the form of the slain human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mh... honestly I always seen it in a different way. Feeding on an animal allow you to take the form of that kind of animal, not the form of that &quot;PARTICULAR&quot; animal. I mean: if you feed on a dog, you can become a dog, not exactly that dog.<br /> According to this point of view, if you you feed on a particular human, you can become an human but you already have an human form.<br /> We don't see the difference between two bears or between two crows but they are not identical and you can take the form of a generic bear or crow.<br /> But this is just my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T06:54:05-07:00","id":866370,"title":"","content":"I think taking people's skin and wearing it could make for a great bloodline concept. It'd be gross, but I could imagine a Nosferatu Bloodline that can wear a skin to temporarily obviate their natural curse with the added benefit of disguising themselves as that person. Could make for a cool and scary bloodline of spies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:54:16-07:00","id":866387,"title":"","content":"No, you can't use Protean to take the form of a human you've killed. Why? Because turning into other people is what Obfuscate does. This is stepping on the toes of another Discipline","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T08:48:15-07:00","id":866397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866370#post866370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think taking people's skin and wearing it could make for a great bloodline concept. It'd be gross, but I could imagine a Nosferatu Bloodline that can wear a skin to temporarily obviate their natural curse with the added benefit of disguising themselves as that person. Could make for a cool and scary bloodline of spies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>know</i> this has been in a vampire book somewhere but I can't remember which one.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's also something a werewolf could do at character generation now, and there's a Tell that mimics the power which a vampire could conceivably have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-16-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T08:50:30-07:00","id":866399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866397#post866397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ''know'' this has been in a vampire book somewhere but I can't remember which one.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's also something a werewolf could do at character generation now, and there's a Tell that mimics the power which a vampire could conceivably have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of an ability the Moulding Room has, where they can wear someone's face.<br /> <br /> There's multiple ways to look like other people, which is sort of where my suggestion for it being a means of obviating their curse by 'being someone else' being the actual main function, with a secondary function of making them good at spying.<br /> <br /> Plus, nosferatu and masks have a bit of a cache since the clanbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:05:39-07:00","id":866934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866180#post866180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mh... honestly I always seen it in a different way. Feeding on an animal allow you to take the form of that kind of animal, not the form of that &quot;PARTICULAR&quot; animal. I mean: if you feed on a dog, you can become a dog, not exactly that dog.<br /> According to this point of view, if you you feed on a particular human, you can become an human but you already have an human form.<br /> We don't see the difference between two bears or between two crows but they are not identical and you can take the form of a generic bear or crow.<br /> But this is just my interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book says that you take on the form of the animal consumed. So i do believe that it is that PARTICULAR animal. Should you consume a wolf with a nasty scar over it's eye. You will have that telling mark too. Or if you are a Male vampire and you consume a female tiger.. Well You have some new parts to deal with. I know it's not super important to the game flow, so you really could have it either way. I just want to throw it out there that I interpret it differently. Crows might all look the same to us humans. But under examination, each and every one of them are different some way, I think of it more like Cloning, you have consumed them, now you are them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:02:24-07:00","id":867669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866037-using-protean-to-steal-the-visage-of-a-human-possible?p=866387#post866387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you can't use Protean to take the form of a human you've killed. Why? Because turning into other people is what Obfuscate does. This is stepping on the toes of another Discipline</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T04:48:20-07:00","id":869224,"title":"","content":"This thread made me think of this great Devotion Pendragon wrote up some time in the past:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/119296-protean-5-dominate-5-devotion?p=119392#post119392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Don the Flesh </b>(Dominate 5, Protean 5)<br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Vitae, 1 Willpower (or 2 Vitae, 1 Willpower if already in Smoke Form)<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Strength + Brawl + Protean vs Stamina + Blood Potency<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite (see text)<br /> <br /> Transforming into a roiling bloody mist the Vampire invades her victim directly, pouring into him through every available orifice. If this victim is resisting this may require a grapple roll, contested by the victim's Strength + Athletics (representing his ability to get away from the cloud). As such the vampire may wish to mesmerize her subject first, before dawning his flesh. Once within the vampire seizes control of her victim's body, taking it wholly as her own as per <i>Possession </i>(Dominate 5). This functions identically to <i>Possession</i>, save for the following additions.<ul><li>The Vampire may use her innate Kindred powers (Physical Intensity, Kindred Senses, Vitae Healing, and Lashing Out) and Disciplines through her victim, with the exception of <i>Possession &amp; </i><i>Primeval Miasma. </i>She pays for all costs with her own Vitae and Willpower, and no unnatural physical alterations persist after she leaves the victim's body.</li> <li>She may feed on the victim from within, using his Blood to fuel her. This damages exactly like feeding, and the Vampire can consume up to her Blood Potency in health levels in a single action. Should she ever find herself without the Vitae to wake while still within her victim's body, the vampire will consume him unconsciously.</li> <li>Unlike <i>Possession</i> Dawn the Flesh does not end when the vampire slumbers. Indeed she may slumber within her victim as most Gangrel slumber within the earth. While she sleeps the victim regains full control over himself and his actions, with only foggy recall of what happened during his possession. A wary victim will likely attempt to expel the vampire, therefore it helps to condition victims with triggers and commands <b>before</b> invading their flesh.</li> </ul><br /> Expelling the Vampire within is extremely difficult. Fire and sunlight do not harm the vampire within, but prolonged exposure to extreme heat may force her into remission (providing a second resistance roll). Barring that exposure to her unique banes can force the Vampire to leave her victim's form, as may certain Kindred abilities (Nightmare or Dominate), and rituals (Blood Sorcery or Scales). In all instances an expelled vampire remains in smoke form unless she deliberately chooses to coalesce.<br /> <i>This Devotion costs 5 Experiences to learn.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}